(i) The family name is the **halogens** (Group VII, also called Group 17).

(ii) At room temperature:

- **Fluorine** is a **gas** (pale yellow);
- **Bromine** is a **liquid** (red-brown, giving off orange-brown fumes);
- **Iodine** is a **solid** (grey-black, giving a purple vapour on heating).

The physical state changes from gas to liquid to solid down the group because the forces between the molecules get stronger as the molecules get bigger.
